    "narrative": "The core of LawDog\u2019s offensive strategy today centers on capitalizing on the favorable matchup against Luis Severino. The standout play of the day is **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts a commanding 80.57 score; he is positioned perfectly in the #2 hole with wind blowing out providing an extra 5% boost to his already elite base projection. Following close behind, **Geraldo Perdomo** (73.81) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53) are high-efficiency anchors. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a strong park factor and a solid matchup against Sugano, while **Luis Arraez** thrives in the friendly confines of today\u2019s venue, effectively neutralizing the threat of the opposing starter. **Jung Hoo Lee** also earns a strong recommendation (68.02) as his lead-off spot combined with the platoon advantage against Severino makes him a primary source for both Runs and SB production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Bryson Stott** (54.18). While he projected as a viable start, he ultimately missed the cut due to his lower position in the batting order and a slight penalty for facing an elite defensive catcher. Our benching of **Gavin Sheets** was more straightforward, as the 2.98 xERA of Logan Gilbert presents a significant barrier that depressed his efficiency score to a marginal 40.86, keeping him well below our starting threshold. We are exercising caution with **Lawrence Butler**, whose score of 53.45 is suppressed by the matchup against McDonald (2.87 xERA). Despite the platoon advantage, the talent of the opposing arm creates a high-risk scenario that necessitates close monitoring. Managers should ensure all lineup configurations are locked before first pitch, as the volatility of these matchups against SPs like McDonald and Soriano could shift the daily efficiency floor rapidly.",
